FORK COMPENSATION REQUIREMENT

Any fork, derivative work, or project that incorporates a substantial portion
of this Software and operates a protocol fee mechanism must remit a
compensation fee to the original project treasury as follows:

  Compensation rate: 0.02% of the protocol fee collected by the fork.

  For example, if the fork charges a protocol fee of 0.02% on each
  transaction, the compensation due is 0.02% × 0.02% = 0.000004 (0.0004%)
  of each transaction's value, payable to the treasury address below.

  Treasury address (Solana):
    BiP5PJuUiXPYCFx98RMCGCnRhdUVrkxSke9C6y2ZohQ9

  Payment must be made in the same SPL token used for the transaction (USDC,
  EURC, or any other accepted mint) and transferred at the time of each
  protocol fee settlement, or batched and settled no less frequently than
  once per calendar month.

  Failure to comply with this clause does not automatically void the MIT
  license grant, but constitutes a breach of this license and may result in
  termination of the rights granted herein at the copyright holder's
  discretion.

